---
// Story: planning/stories/system-as-exhibit.md. Spec: planning/specs/system-as-exhibit.md.
// A demonstration, not a case study about the website — every value below is
// read from the real token source at build time (TokenGallery) and every
// component is the real shared/ui export, live (ComponentGallery). Nothing
// on this page is hand-typed to match the system; it IS the system.
//
// No hero: unlike /about and /process, this page has no media to introduce
// it, so it's PageHeader straight into content, same shell the case-study
// pages use minus ProjectHero. The header carries a back arrow to /about
// (one step back from here in the nav), the same showBack/backHref pair
// [slug].astro uses to get back to the projects grid.
//
// Every section — Overview/Tokens/Components — runs on the site's own
// .section-grid (aside label + body, global.css), the same composition
// /about and every case study use. It used to stack a bare Heading above
// full-width content instead, which is what read as inconsistent next to
// the rest of the site (Max's review).
//
// The lead paragraph (copy-025/026, cut to two sentences copy-028) states
// the page's purpose plainly and stops — the earlier version also framed
// "a Figma-pretty portfolio deletes the code, a GitHub profile deletes the
// taste," but Max asked for shorter and that framing now lives implicitly
// in the Repository card instead (feat-112). It's its own section so it
// stays cuttable without touching the Overview lead or either gallery.
// Repository opens the page rather than closing it (feat-114, Max's
// review) — the "go verify it yourself" proof leads now, ahead of the
// exhibit it backs up, rather than following it.
import Layout from '@app/layouts/Layout.astro';
import { PageHeader } from '@widgets/page-header';
import { TokenGallery } from '@widgets/token-gallery';
import { ComponentGallery } from '@widgets/component-gallery';
import { Heading, CtaCard } from '@shared/ui';
---

<Layout title="System — Max Shturma">
  <main class="system">
    <h1 class="visually-hidden">System</h1>

    <PageHeader title="System" showBack backHref="/about" class="system__header" />

    {
      /* Repository (feat-112, moved to the top per feat-114/Max's review):
        same CtaCard as /about's "System" card, pointed at the public export
        instead. Opens the page rather than closing it now — the "go verify
        it yourself" proof leads, ahead of the tokens/components exhibit it
        backs up.

        Full-bleed, no aside label and no caption (Max's review, round 2):
        every other section keeps the section-grid aside+body split, but this
        one card IS the section — it doesn't need a "Repository" label beside
        it or a supporting line under the heading, so it drops section-grid
        entirely and just runs the full content-container width. Own bg photo
        rather than the shared system-cta.jpg /about's card still uses — a
        flattened export of the composited Figma frame (node 3168:2495): a
        real screenshot of github.com/nimfardo/portfolio-public with its own
        directional gradient scrim already baked in, so `scrim={false}` skips
        CtaCard's default flat one (would otherwise stack and over-darken).
        Heading shortened to 2-3 words on Max's call — "The public repo" read
        generic; "This site's repo" ties it to this exact portfolio. */
    }
    <section class="system__section" data-reveal>
      <CtaCard
        href="https://github.com/nimfardo/portfolio-public"
        image="/media/about/repo-cta.jpg"
        imageAlt=""
        heading="This site's repo"
        scrim={false}
      />
    </section>

    <section class="system__section section-grid">
      <Heading class="section-grid__aside">Overview</Heading>
      <p class="section-grid__body section-prose" data-reveal>
        Design system — the tokens and components this site is built from, live from the
        code. I build in Figma and I ship in code.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="system__section section-grid">
      <Heading class="section-grid__aside">Tokens</Heading>
      <div class="section-grid__body">
        <TokenGallery />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="system__section section-grid">
      <Heading class="section-grid__aside">Components</Heading>
      <div class="section-grid__body">
        <ComponentGallery />
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  /* Same 160px section rhythm as /about and /process. `.system__header` is
     handed to PageHeader as a prop, so it carries THAT component's own
     astro-cid rather than this page's — a scoped rule would silently never
     match (bug-049, the same trap about.astro's header comment documents).
     `:global()` on it for that reason; kept on `.system__section` too even
     though that class sits on a plain <section> in this same file (so a
     scoped rule would already match it) — harmless, and matches the sibling
     rule above rather than mixing scoping styles on adjacent selectors.
     Aside-label spacing is `.section-grid`'s own job now (global.css) — no
     page-local label rule needed.

     Repository is first, straight under PageHeader — this page has no hero
     to carry the 160px rhythm's first hop (unlike /about and /process, whose
     first section's 160px measures from the hero, not the header). PageHeader
     already ships its own 40px margin-bottom, so giving Repository the same
     160px as every other section stacked both and produced a 200px gap under
     the header instead of the site's normal 40px. `:first-of-type` zeroes
     just that one gap and leaves the 160px rhythm intact from Repository
     onward (Max's review).

     Gated to the same >=1024px range PageHeader itself renders at — below
     that PageHeader is `display: none` (widgets/navigation's mobile header
     takes over) and the mobile override two blocks down already gives every
     section, first included, the site's other top offset. */
  .system {
    padding-bottom: 160px;
  }
  /* The 40px side gutter that used to live here moved into PageHeader
     itself (feat-159) — it has to own its own box for the sticky backdrop to
     span the content width. */
  :global(.system__section) {
    padding: 0 40px;
    margin-top: 160px;
  }
  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    :global(.system__section:first-of-type) {
      margin-top: 0;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 1023px) {
    .system {
      padding-bottom: var(--spacing-4xl);
    }
    :global(.system__section) {
      margin-top: var(--spacing-4xl);
    }
  }
</style>
